<title>UK: Vickers quashes Rolls-Royce report.</title>
<headline>Vickers quashes Rolls-Royce report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vickers Plc on Thursday said a newspaper report that Germany's Bayerische Motoren-Werke AG (BMW) had held talks with Vickers about buying its Rolls-Royce car unit was &quot;speculation and rumour&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;Rolls-Royce is a high-performing part of the Vickers portfolio. We have reasearched heavily in research and development and want to see the benefits of that,&quot; a Vickers spokesman said. He noted Rolls-Royce sales were up 12 percent worldwide in 1996.</p>
<p>The Daily Mail report said Rolls-Royce chief Chris Woodwark had met BMW's Walter Hasselkus on Monday.</p>
<p>But the spokesman said meetings between BMW and Rolls Royce were nothing unusual, given the two companies' existing relationship whereby BMW provides engines for the new generation of Rolls-Royce and Bentley cars.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
